WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.113 --> 00:00:18.343
Dr. Craven waited in Colin's room for a long time that afternoon.

2
00:00:19.484 --> 00:00:24.128
Finally the children returned to the house, and he looked Colin over very seriously.

3
00:00:24.148 --> 00:00:27.491
"You shouldn't have stayed out so long," Dr.

4
00:00:27.531 --> 00:00:28.151
Craven said.

5
00:00:28.171 --> 00:00:31.054
"You must not get over tired."

6
00:00:31.074 --> 00:00:33.576
"I'm not tired at all.

7
00:00:34.752 --> 00:00:36.293
Going outside has made me well.

8
00:00:37.373 --> 00:00:40.695
Tomorrow I'm going out in the morning, as well as the afternoon."

9
00:00:41.815 --> 00:00:42.796
The doctor frowned.

10
00:00:42.816 --> 00:00:44.816
"I'm not sure I can allow that.

11
00:00:46.057 --> 00:00:47.678
I'm afraid it would not be wise."

12
00:00:47.698 --> 00:00:51.059
"It would not be wise to try and stop me."

13
00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:55.721
Mary had noticed that Colin had a way of ordering others about.

14
00:00:57.042 --> 00:00:59.483
She had been that way too before she came to Misselthwaite.

15
00:01:00.643 --> 00:01:05.169
But now she knew better, and she felt that she must speak to Colin about his own manners.

16
00:01:06.529 --> 00:01:10.150
After the doctor left, she said, "I feel rather sorry for Dr.

17
00:01:10.190 --> 00:01:12.531
Craven." "So do I.

18
00:01:13.712 --> 00:01:16.012
He won't inherit Misselthwaite now that I'm getting well."

19
00:01:16.032 --> 00:01:20.234
"It must be hard to be polite to a boy who's always rude."

20
00:01:21.474 --> 00:01:22.274
Colin looked up.

21
00:01:22.294 --> 00:01:23.495
"Am I rude?"

22
00:01:23.515 --> 00:01:28.116
"Yes. Nobody has ever dared to do anything you don't like.

23
00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:32.041
Always having your way has made you rude and difficult."

24
00:01:33.241 --> 00:01:34.301
Colin frowned at her.

25
00:01:35.542 --> 00:01:37.562
He didn't like hearing bad things about himself.

26
00:01:37.582 --> 00:01:41.223
"Ben Weatherstaff and I are difficult too."

27
00:01:41.743 --> 00:01:42.764
Mary smiled at him.

28
00:01:42.784 --> 00:01:46.665
"But I'm not as bad as I was before I found the garden."

29
00:01:46.685 --> 00:01:49.966
"I don't want to be difficult, and I won't be."

30
00:01:51.266 --> 00:01:53.287
Now Colin was frowning with determination.

31
00:01:54.507 --> 00:01:55.647
Suddenly he smiled.

32
00:01:55.667 --> 00:02:00.690
"I'll stop being difficult if I go to the secret garden every day.

33
00:02:01.831 --> 00:02:02.811
There's magic in there.

34
00:02:03.031 --> 00:02:03.712
I'm sure of it."

35
00:02:05.433 --> 00:02:06.094
"So am I!"

36
00:02:06.534 --> 00:02:07.094
said Mary.

37
00:02:08.736 --> 00:02:12.538
In the months that followed, it did seem like magic was at work in the garden.

38
00:02:13.799 --> 00:02:17.042
Flowers pushed their way out of the earth and burst into bloom.

39
00:02:18.343 --> 00:02:20.304
The roses were flowering everywhere.

40
00:02:21.545 --> 00:02:25.148
Colin spent hours "watching things growing," as he liked to say.

41
00:02:26.592 --> 00:02:30.295
He watched the insects carrying tiny scraps of straw or food.

42
00:02:31.876 --> 00:02:35.498
Dickon introduced him to the ways of frogs and badgers and fish.

43
00:02:36.799 --> 00:02:39.380
There were so many things to look at in the secret garden.

44
00:02:40.581 --> 00:02:45.124
Colin began to believe there was magic not only in the garden but also in him.

45
00:02:45.144 --> 00:02:48.466
"Come, everyone," he said one day.

46
00:02:48.486 --> 00:02:50.908
"Stand here in a line."

47
00:02:52.584 --> 00:02:56.747
Mary, Dickon, and Ben stopped working in the garden and stood in front of Colin.

48
00:02:57.868 --> 00:03:02.691
"When I grow up, I am going to make great scientific discoveries," announced Colin.

49
00:03:02.711 --> 00:03:06.014
"I am going to begin now with this experiment.

50
00:03:07.255 --> 00:03:11.137
The magic in this garden has made me stand up and know that I'm going to live.

51
00:03:12.899 --> 00:03:17.042
Now I'm going to try to put more magic into myself so that I will grow strong.

52
00:03:18.282 --> 00:03:20.064
I don't know how to do this for sure.

53
00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:25.141
But perhaps if I keep thinking about it and calling it, the magic will come."

54
00:03:25.161 --> 00:03:27.422
"How will you do that?"

55
00:03:28.022 --> 00:03:28.702
asked Mary.

56
00:03:28.722 --> 00:03:35.164
"Every day, as often as I can, I'm going to say: 'Magic is in me!

57
00:03:36.424 --> 00:03:37.885
Magic is making me well!

58
00:03:39.085 --> 00:03:40.886
I am going to be as strong as Dickon!'

59
00:03:42.066 --> 00:03:42.986
And you must say it too.

60
00:03:44.187 --> 00:03:45.547
Will you help me, Ben Weatherstaff?"

61
00:03:46.787 --> 00:03:48.588
"Yes," said the old gardener.

62
00:03:49.908 --> 00:03:51.488
"And now I'd like to see you walk."

63
00:03:53.009 --> 00:03:55.109
Colin set off with Dickon at his side.

64
00:03:56.210 --> 00:03:59.931
Mary and Ben followed along behind, as if they were in a parade.

65
00:04:01.211 --> 00:04:03.912
It was a parade that moved slowly but with dignity.

66
00:04:05.132 --> 00:04:07.093
Every few yards it stopped to rest.

67
00:04:08.353 --> 00:04:11.854
Colin leaned on Dickon's arm, but sometimes he walked by himself.

68
00:04:11.874 --> 00:04:14.755
"The magic is in me!"

69
00:04:15.135 --> 00:04:15.875
he kept saying.

70
00:04:15.895 --> 00:04:18.836
"The magic is making me strong!"

71
00:04:20.108 --> 00:04:21.969
They walked all around the garden.

72
00:04:21.989 --> 00:04:23.669
"I did it!

73
00:04:24.109 --> 00:04:24.930
The magic worked!"

74
00:04:25.390 --> 00:04:26.630
Colin exclaimed at the end.

75
00:04:27.950 --> 00:04:28.631
"What will Dr.

76
00:04:28.691 --> 00:04:29.551
Craven say?"

77
00:04:29.911 --> 00:04:30.571
asked Mary.

78
00:04:30.591 --> 00:04:35.813
"He won't say anything," said Colin, "because he won't be told.

79
00:04:36.993 --> 00:04:38.754
This will be the biggest secret of all.

80
00:04:39.974 --> 00:04:43.195
Every day I will go to and from the garden in my wheelchair.

81
00:04:44.355 --> 00:04:46.216
I won't have the servants whispering about me.

82
00:04:47.424 --> 00:04:51.007
I won't let my father hear about it until the experiment has succeeded.

83
00:04:52.188 --> 00:04:57.112
Then one day I will walk into his study and show him that I'm just like any other

84
00:04:57.192 --> 00:05:01.456
boy." "He'll think he's dreaming," said Mary.

85
00:05:01.476 --> 00:05:04.038
"He won't believe his eyes."

86
00:05:04.058 --> 00:05:08.902
"You'll grow so strong that you'll soon be boxing," said Ben.

87
00:05:08.922 --> 00:05:13.226
"You'll end up being the champion prizefighter of all England."

88
00:05:14.507 --> 00:05:15.528
Colin frowned at him.

89
00:05:16.808 --> 00:05:18.470
"No, Weatherstaff, that's not true.

90
00:05:20.011 --> 00:05:23.575
No matter how well the magic works, I will not be a prizefighter.

91
00:05:24.656 --> 00:05:26.678
I will be a scientific discoverer."

92
00:05:26.698 --> 00:05:30.461
"Oh, pardon, sir," said Ben.

93
00:05:30.481 --> 00:05:33.985
"I should have known it wasn't a joking matter."

94
00:05:35.146 --> 00:05:36.327
But his eyes twinkled.

95
00:05:37.628 --> 00:05:41.372
He could tell that Colin was already gaining strength and spirit.
